CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*node)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct coresight_path)...)
#165: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-core.c:1066:
+	node = kzalloc(sizeof(struct coresight_path), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!path"
#251: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-core.c:1167:
+	if (path == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

